###Pure

// ============================================================================================
// firm_balance_sheet -- the balance sheet, five levels above core-types
// ============================================================================================
// LAYER 3, the deepest project in the graph. Three declared dependencies:
//
//    pnl-attribution   layer 2  (position-keeping, valuation-core)
//    exposure-agg      layer 2  (credit-core, collateral-core)
//    liquidity-view    layer 2  (cash-core, funding-core)
//
// Their transitive closure is seventeen projects and everything in it is VISIBLE here:
// CT_CURRENCY, CP_LEGAL_ENTITY, CI_INSTRUMENT, CA_ACCOUNT all arrive by two or three routes.
// Not one of them is named anywhere in this project. Every fact taken from below layer 2 is
// reached THROUGH one of the three declared dependencies -- `$line.netExposure.counterparty`
// gets to a legal entity without this file ever writing `core_party`, and a currency is a
// three-character String here because `core_types::CtCurrency` belongs to somebody else's
// declaration. That restraint is the whole point of the depth: a reference from here is five
// hops from a leaf, and an undeclared one would still compile in the full graph and fail the
// moment the project is compiled with its own closure.
//
// WHAT A BALANCE SHEET IS FOR. Assets on one side, liabilities and equity on the other, and
// the two sides equal because they are the same money counted twice -- once by what the firm
// holds and once by whose it is. Everything below exists to make that identity survive
// contact with a bank:
//
//   MEASUREMENT BASIS. The same bond is three different numbers depending on why it is held.
//   Amortised cost if it is held to collect, FVOCI if it is held to collect and to sell,
//   FVTPL if neither. The basis is not a presentational choice; it decides whether a price
//   move lands in profit, in reserves, or nowhere at all.
//
//   THE BOOK BOUNDARY. Trading book against banking book. The trading book is marked daily
//   and its moves are pnl-attribution's subject; the banking book is accrued and its moves
//   are provisions. A position moving across the boundary is a capital event.
//
//   DERIVATIVES BEFORE NETTING. Gross positive value is an asset, gross negative value is a
//   liability, and both are enormous. What nets is a legal question answered by
//   exposure-agg's netting sets, not an accounting one, and the balance sheet shows the
//   gross AND the offset so a reader can see which regime produced the number.
//
//   HQLA BY LEVEL. The liquidity buffer is a subset of the assets, sliced by a different
//   taxonomy (L1 / L2A / L2B, after haircut, after cap) than the statement uses. This
//   project holds the bridge between the two, which is why it depends on liquidity-view.
//
//   GOODWILL AND THE DEDUCTIONS. Goodwill is an asset that carries no capital. So are most
//   intangibles, deferred tax on losses, and holdings in other financials over a threshold.
//   The deduction table is the list of things on the left-hand side that regulators refuse
//   to count, and it is the honest half of every capital ratio.
//
//   PROVISIONS. Money already lost and not yet paid out -- expected credit losses by stage,
//   litigation, restructuring. Opening plus charge less utilisation less release is closing,
//   and the balance-sheet number is only the last of those five.
//
//   AND THE EQUITY THAT BALANCES IT. Share capital, retained earnings, OCI reserves,
//   non-controlling interests. It is a residual by construction, and every arithmetic error
//   anywhere above lands in it.
//
// CONSTRUCTS. An AGGREGATION shape -- four `~groupBy` views totalling the line table at four
// widths, of which `FBS_SIDE_TOTAL` is literally the balance check -- and a SCHEMA of this
// project's own, `fbs`, so a statement cannot be confused with a trading table by a DBA, a
// backup policy, or a downstream mapping.
//
// No enums, no profiles, no functions, no associations, no ###Data, no Runtime.

// -------------------------------------------------------------------- the statement itself

// FOR: the header of one balance sheet -- one institution, one date, one reporting currency.
// Everything else in this project hangs off this key. The three totals are STORED because
// they are what was published; `balanceDifference()` recomputes nothing and instead states
// the identity that must hold, so a published statement that does not balance says so.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsBalanceSheet
[
   assetsArePositive: $this.totalAssets > 0.0
]
{
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   reportingCurrency: String[1];
   basisOfPreparation: String[1];
   consolidationScope: String[1];
   statementStatus: String[1];
   runId: String[0..1];
   pnlAttributionId: String[0..1];
   nsfrScenarioCurrency: String[0..1];
   totalAssets: Float[1];
   totalLiabilities: Float[1];
   totalEquity: Float[1];
   preparedBy: String[0..1];
   preparedAt: DateTime[0..1];
   signedOffOn: StrictDate[0..1];

   run: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBalanceSheetRun[0..1];
   lines: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[*];
   sideTotals: firm_balance_sheet::FbsSideTotal[*];
   categoryTotals: firm_balance_sheet::FbsCategoryTotal[*];
   balanceChecks: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBalanceCheck[*];
   attestations: firm_balance_sheet::FbsAttestation[*];
   retainedEarnings: firm_balance_sheet::FbsRetainedEarnings[0..1];
   hqlaStock: firm_balance_sheet::FbsHqlaStock[*];
   equityBalances: firm_balance_sheet::FbsEquityBalance[*];

   // Straight into pnl-attribution's own `~groupBy` view: the firm's whole day of P&L as one
   // row, without reading a P&L line. This is the join that makes the movement in retained
   // earnings checkable against the movement in market value.
   pnlRunTotal: pnl_attribution::PnlRunTotal[0..1];
   // And into liquidity-view's one-year ratio, on institution, currency and date.
   nsfrResult: liquidity_view::LqvNsfrResult[0..1];

   // The identity. Zero, or somebody has some explaining to do.
   balanceDifference() { $this.totalAssets - ($this.totalLiabilities + $this.totalEquity) } : Float[1];
   isBalanced() { ($this.totalAssets - ($this.totalLiabilities + $this.totalEquity))->abs() < 1.0 } : Boolean[1];
   // Equity over assets. The crudest solvency number there is and still the first one read.
   equityRatio() { $this.totalEquity / $this.totalAssets } : Float[1];
   leverageMultiple() { $this.totalAssets / $this.totalEquity } : Float[1];
   isPublished() { $this.signedOffOn->isNotEmpty() } : Boolean[1];
   statementKey() { $this.institutionId + '/' + $this.reportingCurrency } : String[1];
}

// FOR: the batch that produced a statement. An incomplete run is a run whose numbers must
// not be read, and it names the two upstream runs it consumed so a disagreement can be
// traced to which of them moved.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsBalanceSheetRun
{
   runId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   runType: String[1];
   runStatus: String[1];
   startedAt: DateTime[0..1];
   completedAt: DateTime[0..1];
   lineCount: Integer[0..1];
   rejectedLineCount: Integer[0..1];
   exposureRunId: String[0..1];
   pnlAttributionId: String[0..1];
   triggeredBy: String[0..1];

   statements: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBalanceSheet[*];
   lines: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[*];
   // The two upstream batches, named rather than copied.
   pnlRun: pnl_attribution::PnlAttributionRun[0..1];
   exposureRun: exposure_agg::ExaExposureRun[0..1];

   isComplete() { $this.runStatus == 'COMPLETE' } : Boolean[1];
   rejectedPct() { ($this.rejectedLineCount->orElse(0)->toFloat() * 100.0) / $this.lineCount->orElse(1)->toFloat() } : Float[1];
}

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------- the line grain

// FOR: one line of the statement -- the grain everything totals from, and the ROOT of a
// filter-subtype family split three ways by which side of the sheet the row is on. The
// measurement basis, the book and the fair-value level all live here because they are
// properties of the LINE and not of the instrument: the same bond in two books is two rows
// carrying two bases.
//
// `carryingAmount` is what appears in the statement. `grossAmount` less `impairmentAmount`
// should reproduce it, and where it does not an adjustment was posted.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem
{
   lineId: String[1];
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   reportingCurrency: String[1];
   side: String[1];
   categoryCode: String[1];
   basisCode: String[1];
   bookCode: String[1];
   fairValueLevel: String[0..1];
   carryingAmount: Float[1];
   grossAmount: Float[0..1];
   impairmentAmount: Float[0..1];
   priorCarryingAmount: Float[0..1];
   localCurrency: String[0..1];
   localAmount: Float[0..1];
   fxRate: Float[0..1];
   runId: String[0..1];

   statement: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBalanceSheet[0..1];
   category: firm_balance_sheet::FbsCategory[0..1];
   basis: firm_balance_sheet::FbsMeasurementBasis[0..1];
   book: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBookClassification[0..1];
   valuationLevel: firm_balance_sheet::FbsFairValueLevel[0..1];
   run: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBalanceSheetRun[0..1];
   adjustments: firm_balance_sheet::FbsAccountingAdjustment[*];
   categoryTotal: firm_balance_sheet::FbsCategoryTotal[0..1];
   basisTotal: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBasisTotal[0..1];
   bookTotal: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBookTotal[0..1];
   sideTotal: firm_balance_sheet::FbsSideTotal[0..1];
   // Out of this project: the credit system's view of the same balance, where there is one.
   netExposure: exposure_agg::ExaNetExposure[0..1];

   netAmount() { $this.grossAmount->orElse($this.carryingAmount) - $this.impairmentAmount->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   movement() { $this.carryingAmount - $this.priorCarryingAmount->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   movementPct() { ($this.carryingAmount - $this.priorCarryingAmount->orElse(0.0)) / $this.priorCarryingAmount->orElse(1.0) } : Float[1];
   // The stated carrying amount against gross-less-impairment. Non-zero means an adjustment.
   impairmentCheck() { $this.carryingAmount - ($this.grossAmount->orElse($this.carryingAmount) - $this.impairmentAmount->orElse(0.0)) } : Float[1];
   coverageRatio() { $this.impairmentAmount->orElse(0.0) / $this.grossAmount->orElse(1.0) } : Float[1];
   isAsset() { $this.side == 'ASSET' } : Boolean[1];
   isFairValued() { $this.basisCode == 'FVTPL' || $this.basisCode == 'FVOCI' } : Boolean[1];
   isTradingBook() { $this.bookCode == 'TRADING' } : Boolean[1];
   // Back into the currency the ledger actually posts in.
   reportingFromLocal() { $this.localAmount->orElse(0.0) * $this.fxRate->orElse(1.0) } : Float[1];
   lineKey() { $this.institutionId + '/' + $this.categoryCode + '/' + $this.lineId } : String[1];
}

// FOR: the left-hand side. Adds only what an asset has and a liability does not -- whether
// the row is part of the liquidity buffer, how much of it is pledged away, and how many days
// it would take to turn into cash. `~filter FbsAssetRows`, SIDE = 'ASSET'.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsAssetLine extends firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem
{
   isHqla: Boolean[0..1];
   hqlaLevelCode: String[0..1];
   encumberedAmount: Float[0..1];
   liquidityDays: Integer[0..1];
   hqlaHoldingId: String[0..1];

   // The holding as liquidity-view knows it: same asset, different taxonomy, different
   // haircut. The two numbers are allowed to differ and the difference is the point.
   hqlaHolding: liquidity_view::LqvHqlaHolding[0..1];

   // What is actually free. A pledged asset is on the balance sheet and not in the buffer.
   unencumberedAmount() { $this.carryingAmount - $this.encumberedAmount->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   encumbranceRatio() { $this.encumberedAmount->orElse(0.0) / $this.carryingAmount } : Float[1];
   isLiquidWithinMonth() { $this.liquidityDays->orElse(999) <= 30 } : Boolean[1];
}

// FOR: the right-hand side above the line. What the firm owes, when it falls due, whether it
// is secured, and to whom -- the three facts that decide whether a liability is funding or a
// run risk. `~filter FbsLiabilityRows`, SIDE = 'LIABILITY'.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsLiabilityLine extends firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem
{
   maturityDate: StrictDate[0..1];
   isSecured: Boolean[0..1];
   fundingType: String[0..1];
   counterpartyId: String[0..1];
   isDemandDeposit: Boolean[0..1];

   isPerpetual() { $this.maturityDate->isEmpty() } : Boolean[1];
   isCallableFunding() { $this.isDemandDeposit->orElse(false) || $this.maturityDate->isEmpty() } : Boolean[1];
}

// FOR: the right-hand side below the line -- the residual. Carries which equity component
// the row rolls into and whether the regulator lets it count as CET1, which are two
// different questions with two different answers for the same share.
// `~filter FbsEquityRows`, SIDE = 'EQUITY'.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsEquityLine extends firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem
{
   equityComponentCode: String[0..1];
   isCet1Eligible: Boolean[0..1];
   nonControllingInterest: Float[0..1];

   attributableToParent() { $this.carryingAmount - $this.nonControllingInterest->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   countsAsCet1() { $this.isCet1Eligible->orElse(false) } : Boolean[1];
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------- the classifiers

// FOR: the statement taxonomy -- where a line prints, in what order, under which note.
// `parentCode` is a plain String and not a resolved parent: a self-join would let a reader
// walk the hierarchy in SQL, and a balance-sheet taxonomy is small enough that walking it
// in the model is cheaper than the join it would cost every query that does not.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsCategory
{
   categoryCode: String[1];
   categoryName: String[1];
   parentCode: String[0..1];
   side: String[1];
   statementOrder: Integer[0..1];
   isSubtotal: Boolean[0..1];
   noteReference: String[0..1];
   retiredOn: StrictDate[0..1];

   lines: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[*];
   totals: firm_balance_sheet::FbsCategoryTotal[*];

   isTopLevel() { $this.parentCode->isEmpty() } : Boolean[1];
   isLive() { $this.retiredOn->isEmpty() } : Boolean[1];
}

// FOR: how a line was measured, which decides where its movements go. AC, FVOCI, FVTPL.
// `movementsThrough` is the whole of IFRS 9 in one column: P&L, OCI, or nowhere.
// `recyclesToPl` is the difference between an FVOCI debt instrument and an FVOCI equity one,
// and it is why the same three letters mean two things.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsMeasurementBasis
{
   basisCode: String[1];
   basisName: String[1];
   standardReference: String[0..1];
   movementsThrough: String[1];
   isFairValue: Boolean[1];
   requiresEcl: Boolean[0..1];
   recyclesToPl: Boolean[0..1];

   lines: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[*];
   basisTotals: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBasisTotal[*];
   ociReserves: firm_balance_sheet::FbsOciReserve[*];

   isAmortisedCost() { $this.basisCode == 'AC' } : Boolean[1];
   hitsProfitAndLoss() { $this.movementsThrough == 'PL' } : Boolean[1];
   hitsOtherComprehensiveIncome() { $this.movementsThrough == 'OCI' } : Boolean[1];
}

// FOR: the trading book / banking book boundary. Intent, not instrument: the boundary is a
// policy document, and `boundaryPolicyRef` names it because moving a position across is an
// event a regulator will ask about by reference.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsBookClassification
{
   bookCode: String[1];
   bookName: String[1];
   intent: String[1];
   isTrading: Boolean[1];
   defaultBasisCode: String[0..1];
   capitalTreatment: String[0..1];
   boundaryPolicyRef: String[0..1];

   defaultBasis: firm_balance_sheet::FbsMeasurementBasis[0..1];
   lines: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[*];
   bookTotals: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBookTotal[*];

   isMarkedDaily() { $this.isTrading } : Boolean[1];
   usesMarketRisk() { $this.capitalTreatment == 'MARKET_RISK' } : Boolean[1];
}

// FOR: the fair-value hierarchy, Level 1 to Level 3. What it is FOR is disclosure: a firm
// with a large Level 3 book is telling you that a material part of its assets is worth
// whatever its own model says, and the level is the only column that admits it.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsFairValueLevel
{
   levelCode: String[1];
   levelName: String[1];
   inputType: String[1];
   isObservable: Boolean[1];
   requiresDisclosure: Boolean[0..1];
   levelRank: Integer[0..1];

   lines: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[*];

   isModelled() { $this.levelCode == 'L3' } : Boolean[1];
}

// --------------------------------------------------------- trading book vs banking book

// FOR: the trading-book detail behind a fair-valued line -- and the point in this project
// where the balance sheet meets pnl-attribution at its own grain. The five columns of
// `Fbs_TradingPositionPnlLine` are exactly pnl-attribution's key, so `pnlLine` reaches the
// day's explain for this position: what the balance sheet carries and why it moved, side by
// side, without either project restating the other's arithmetic.
//
// The two reserves are the honest part: a mid-market fair value is not a realisable one, and
// bid-offer and model reserves are what comes off before the number is published.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsTradingBookPosition
{
   lineId: String[1];
   institutionId: String[1];
   accountNo: String[0..1];
   instrumentId: String[0..1];
   cobDate: StrictDate[0..1];
   pnlAttributionId: String[0..1];
   quantity: Float[0..1];
   fairValue: Float[1];
   dayOneProfit: Float[0..1];
   bidOfferReserve: Float[0..1];
   modelReserve: Float[0..1];
   isLong: Boolean[0..1];
   deskCode: String[0..1];

   line: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[0..1];
   // THE DEEP JOIN: five columns into PNL_LINE, which is itself the apex of
   // pnl-attribution's own diamond over position-keeping and valuation-core.
   pnlLine: pnl_attribution::PnlLine[0..1];

   totalReserve() { $this.bidOfferReserve->orElse(0.0) + $this.modelReserve->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   prudentValue() { $this.fairValue - ($this.bidOfferReserve->orElse(0.0) + $this.modelReserve->orElse(0.0)) } : Float[1];
   reservePct() { ($this.bidOfferReserve->orElse(0.0) + $this.modelReserve->orElse(0.0)) / $this.fairValue } : Float[1];
   isShort() { $this.isLong->orElse(true) == false } : Boolean[1];
}

// FOR: the banking-book detail behind an amortised-cost line. A loan is not a price, it is a
// schedule: gross carrying amount, the effective interest rate that unwinds the premium, the
// accrued interest nobody has paid yet, and the allowance that says how much of it will
// never arrive. The IFRS 9 stage is the single column that decides whether that allowance is
// twelve-month or lifetime.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsBankingBookAsset
{
   lineId: String[1];
   productType: String[1];
   originationDate: StrictDate[0..1];
   maturityDate: StrictDate[0..1];
   grossCarryingAmount: Float[1];
   effectiveInterestRate: Float[0..1];
   unamortisedPremium: Float[0..1];
   accruedInterest: Float[0..1];
   eclStage: Integer[0..1];
   allowanceAmount: Float[0..1];
   isPurchasedCreditImpaired: Boolean[0..1];
   netExposureId: String[0..1];

   line: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[0..1];
   eclAllowances: firm_balance_sheet::FbsEclAllowance[*];
   // The credit system's number for the same borrower, reached through exposure-agg.
   netExposure: exposure_agg::ExaNetExposure[0..1];

   netCarryingAmount() { $this.grossCarryingAmount - $this.allowanceAmount->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   amortisedCostWithAccrual() { ($this.grossCarryingAmount - $this.allowanceAmount->orElse(0.0)) + $this.accruedInterest->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   coverageRatio() { $this.allowanceAmount->orElse(0.0) / $this.grossCarryingAmount } : Float[1];
   isCreditImpaired() { $this.eclStage->orElse(1) == 3 } : Boolean[1];
   isLifetimeEcl() { $this.eclStage->orElse(1) >= 2 } : Boolean[1];
}

// ------------------------------------------------------- derivatives, before any netting

// FOR: a derivative carried as an ASSET at its gross positive fair value, before a single
// offset. This is the number that makes a bank's balance sheet look the size it does, and it
// is the number IFRS requires unless the offset criteria are met. CVA comes off it because
// the counterparty may not pay; FVA because funding the position is not free.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsDerivativeAsset
{
   derivativeAssetId: String[1];
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   nettingSetId: String[0..1];
   netExposureId: String[0..1];
   counterpartyId: String[0..1];
   productClass: String[1];
   notional: Float[0..1];
   grossPositiveValue: Float[1];
   cvaAdjustment: Float[0..1];
   fvaAdjustment: Float[0..1];
   isCleared: Boolean[0..1];
   currency: String[0..1];
   lineId: String[0..1];

   line: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[0..1];
   netting: firm_balance_sheet::FbsNettingAdjustment[0..1];
   // exposure-agg's netting set is the LEGAL answer to what may be offset. This project does
   // not re-derive enforceability; it reads it.
   nettingSet: exposure_agg::ExaNettingSet[0..1];
   netExposure: exposure_agg::ExaNetExposure[0..1];
   // Straight into exposure-agg's `~groupBy` view: this counterparty's whole day, one row.
   counterpartyDayNet: exposure_agg::ExaCounterpartyDayNet[0..1];

   carryingValue() { $this.grossPositiveValue - ($this.cvaAdjustment->orElse(0.0) + $this.fvaAdjustment->orElse(0.0)) } : Float[1];
   totalValuationAdjustment() { $this.cvaAdjustment->orElse(0.0) + $this.fvaAdjustment->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   cvaPct() { $this.cvaAdjustment->orElse(0.0) / $this.grossPositiveValue } : Float[1];
   isBilateral() { $this.isCleared->orElse(false) == false } : Boolean[1];
}

// FOR: the same trade seen from the other side of zero -- a derivative carried as a
// LIABILITY at its gross negative value. It exists as its own class rather than a sign on
// the asset because the balance sheet presents the two separately and the netting that
// collapses them is an event with its own row.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsDerivativeLiability
{
   derivativeLiabilityId: String[1];
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   nettingSetId: String[0..1];
   netExposureId: String[0..1];
   counterpartyId: String[0..1];
   productClass: String[1];
   notional: Float[0..1];
   grossNegativeValue: Float[1];
   dvaAdjustment: Float[0..1];
   fvaAdjustment: Float[0..1];
   isCleared: Boolean[0..1];
   currency: String[0..1];
   lineId: String[0..1];

   line: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[0..1];
   netting: firm_balance_sheet::FbsNettingAdjustment[0..1];
   nettingSet: exposure_agg::ExaNettingSet[0..1];
   netExposure: exposure_agg::ExaNetExposure[0..1];

   // DVA is the gain a firm books because its own credit got worse. Subtracting it from a
   // liability is arithmetically identical to and morally distinct from everything else here.
   carryingValue() { $this.grossNegativeValue - ($this.dvaAdjustment->orElse(0.0) + $this.fvaAdjustment->orElse(0.0)) } : Float[1];
   dvaPct() { $this.dvaAdjustment->orElse(0.0) / $this.grossNegativeValue } : Float[1];
   isBilateral() { $this.isCleared->orElse(false) == false } : Boolean[1];
}

// FOR: what actually nets, per netting set per day. Gross both ways, the offset applied, net
// both ways. `offsetBasis` records WHICH regime allowed it -- IAS 32 is stricter than
// US GAAP's ASC 815-10-45, and the same book is a different size under each, which is the
// single largest reconciling item between a European and an American balance sheet.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsNettingAdjustment
{
   nettingSetId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   institutionId: String[1];
   grossAssetAmount: Float[1];
   grossLiabilityAmount: Float[1];
   offsetAmount: Float[1];
   netAssetAmount: Float[0..1];
   netLiabilityAmount: Float[0..1];
   isBalanceSheetNetted: Boolean[0..1];
   offsetBasis: String[0..1];
   legalOpinionRef: String[0..1];

   derivativeAssets: firm_balance_sheet::FbsDerivativeAsset[*];
   derivativeLiabilities: firm_balance_sheet::FbsDerivativeLiability[*];
   collateralOffsets: firm_balance_sheet::FbsCollateralOffset[*];
   nettingSet: exposure_agg::ExaNettingSet[0..1];

   // The balance-sheet shrinkage the legal opinion buys, in money.
   balanceSheetReduction() { $this.offsetAmount * 2.0 } : Float[1];
   assetAfterOffset() { $this.grossAssetAmount - $this.offsetAmount } : Float[1];
   liabilityAfterOffset() { $this.grossLiabilityAmount - $this.offsetAmount } : Float[1];
   offsetPct() { $this.offsetAmount / $this.grossAssetAmount } : Float[1];
   // Stated net against recomputed net. Non-zero means somebody offset something twice.
   netAssetCheck() { $this.netAssetAmount->orElse($this.grossAssetAmount - $this.offsetAmount) - ($this.grossAssetAmount - $this.offsetAmount) } : Float[1];
   isNettedOnBalanceSheet() { $this.isBalanceSheetNetted->orElse(false) } : Boolean[1];
}

// FOR: collateral taken against a derivative, and how much of it the balance sheet is
// allowed to offset. Cash offsets and securities generally do not, which is why both amounts
// are held and only one of them feeds `offsetAppliedAmount`. `rehypothecatedAmount` is the
// part that has been lent on again and is therefore somebody else's asset too.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsCollateralOffset
{
   offsetId: String[1];
   nettingSetId: String[1];
   positionId: String[0..1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   cashCollateralAmount: Float[0..1];
   securitiesCollateralAmount: Float[0..1];
   offsetAppliedAmount: Float[1];
   isCash: Boolean[0..1];
   currency: String[0..1];
   rehypothecatedAmount: Float[0..1];

   netting: firm_balance_sheet::FbsNettingAdjustment[0..1];
   // exposure-agg's collateral position, haircut and all.
   collateralPosition: exposure_agg::ExaCollateralPosition[0..1];

   totalCollateral() { $this.cashCollateralAmount->orElse(0.0) + $this.securitiesCollateralAmount->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   // What was taken but could not be offset. Still on the balance sheet, both sides.
   ineligibleAmount() { ($this.cashCollateralAmount->orElse(0.0) + $this.securitiesCollateralAmount->orElse(0.0)) - $this.offsetAppliedAmount } : Float[1];
   offsetEfficiency() { $this.offsetAppliedAmount / ($this.cashCollateralAmount->orElse(0.0) + $this.securitiesCollateralAmount->orElse(1.0)) } : Float[1];
   isRehypothecated() { $this.rehypothecatedAmount->orElse(0.0) > 0.0 } : Boolean[1];
}

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------- HQLA by level

// FOR: the bridge between the balance sheet's assets and the liquidity buffer, at the grain
// liquidity-view reports on -- one institution, one date, one HQLA level, one currency. The
// balance-sheet amount and the weighted amount are BOTH held because they are different
// numbers for the same assets: the statement counts them at carrying value, the LCR counts
// them after haircut and after the L2 cap, and the gap between the two is the reason this
// project depends on liquidity-view at all.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsHqlaStock
{
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   hqlaLevelCode: String[1];
   reportingCurrency: String[1];
   balanceSheetAmount: Float[1];
   unencumberedAmount: Float[0..1];
   haircutAmount: Float[0..1];
   weightedAmount: Float[1];
   capExcessAmount: Float[0..1];
   holdingCount: Integer[0..1];
   scenarioId: String[0..1];

   statement: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBalanceSheet[0..1];
   // liquidity-view's own definitions: the level with its standard haircut and cap, and the
   // ratio the buffer was built for.
   level: liquidity_view::LqvHqlaLevel[0..1];
   lcrResult: liquidity_view::LqvLcrResult[0..1];

   // How much of the balance-sheet amount survives to the buffer.
   recognisedPct() { ($this.weightedAmount * 100.0) / $this.balanceSheetAmount } : Float[1];
   haircutPct() { ($this.haircutAmount->orElse(0.0) * 100.0) / $this.balanceSheetAmount } : Float[1];
   // What the cap threw away. Real assets, real liquidity, no regulatory credit.
   cappedAway() { $this.capExcessAmount->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   isLevelOne() { $this.hqlaLevelCode == 'L1' } : Boolean[1];
   averageHoldingSize() { $this.balanceSheetAmount / $this.holdingCount->orElse(1)->toFloat() } : Float[1];
}

// ------------------------------------------- goodwill, intangibles and what never counts

// FOR: goodwill, per cash-generating unit. What it is FOR, honestly, is being tested: it is
// the amount by which an acquisition cost more than the things it bought, it never
// amortises, and it sits there until an impairment test says it does not. `recoverableAmount`
// against `carryingAmount` IS the test, and `discountRate` is the assumption the whole answer
// turns on.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsGoodwill
{
   goodwillId: String[1];
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   cashGeneratingUnit: String[1];
   acquisitionDate: StrictDate[0..1];
   grossGoodwill: Float[1];
   accumulatedImpairment: Float[0..1];
   carryingAmount: Float[1];
   recoverableAmount: Float[0..1];
   lastTestedOn: StrictDate[0..1];
   discountRate: Float[0..1];
   lineId: String[0..1];

   line: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[0..1];
   deductions: firm_balance_sheet::FbsCapitalDeduction[*];

   // Positive means the unit is worth less than the books say and an impairment is due.
   headroom() { $this.recoverableAmount->orElse(0.0) - $this.carryingAmount } : Float[1];
   isImpaired() { $this.recoverableAmount->orElse(0.0) < $this.carryingAmount } : Boolean[1];
   impairmentToDatePct() { ($this.accumulatedImpairment->orElse(0.0) * 100.0) / $this.grossGoodwill } : Float[1];
   isTested() { $this.lastTestedOn->isNotEmpty() } : Boolean[1];
}

// FOR: everything else with no physical form -- capitalised software, customer lists,
// licences. Distinguished from goodwill because these DO amortise, and distinguished from
// each other by `isInternallyGenerated`, which is the column that decides whether the cost
// was allowed onto the balance sheet at all.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsIntangibleAsset
{
   intangibleId: String[1];
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   intangibleType: String[1];
   costAmount: Float[1];
   accumulatedAmortisation: Float[0..1];
   carryingAmount: Float[1];
   usefulLifeYears: Integer[0..1];
   isInternallyGenerated: Boolean[0..1];
   lineId: String[0..1];

   line: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[0..1];
   deductions: firm_balance_sheet::FbsCapitalDeduction[*];

   netBookValue() { $this.costAmount - $this.accumulatedAmortisation->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   amortisedPct() { ($this.accumulatedAmortisation->orElse(0.0) * 100.0) / $this.costAmount } : Float[1];
   annualCharge() { $this.costAmount / $this.usefulLifeYears->orElse(1)->toFloat() } : Float[1];
   isFullyAmortised() { $this.accumulatedAmortisation->orElse(0.0) >= $this.costAmount } : Boolean[1];
}

// FOR: the assets that never make it into capital. This is the reconciling table between
// accounting equity and regulatory capital, and it is the honest half of every ratio: an
// intangible is a real asset and worth nothing in a resolution, so it comes straight off
// CET1. Some deductions are absolute, some only bite above a threshold and the remainder is
// risk-weighted instead, which is why both `deductedAmount` and `riskWeightedRemainder`
// exist on one row.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsCapitalDeduction
{
   deductionId: String[1];
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   deductionCode: String[1];
   deductionTier: String[1];
   balanceSheetAmount: Float[1];
   thresholdAmount: Float[0..1];
   deductedAmount: Float[1];
   riskWeightedRemainder: Float[0..1];
   regulationReference: String[0..1];
   isFullyDeducted: Boolean[0..1];
   goodwillId: String[0..1];
   intangibleId: String[0..1];
   lineId: String[0..1];

   line: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[0..1];
   goodwill: firm_balance_sheet::FbsGoodwill[0..1];
   intangible: firm_balance_sheet::FbsIntangibleAsset[0..1];

   // What the balance sheet keeps and capital does not.
   retainedOnBalanceSheet() { $this.balanceSheetAmount - $this.deductedAmount } : Float[1];
   deductionPct() { ($this.deductedAmount * 100.0) / $this.balanceSheetAmount } : Float[1];
   excessOverThreshold() { $this.balanceSheetAmount - $this.thresholdAmount->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   isThresholdDeduction() { $this.thresholdAmount->isNotEmpty() } : Boolean[1];
   hitsCommonEquity() { $this.deductionTier == 'CET1' } : Boolean[1];
}

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------- provisions

// FOR: money already lost and not yet paid out. The balance-sheet number is `closingBalance`
// and it is the least interesting of the five: opening plus charge less utilised less
// released is the ROLL-FORWARD, and a provision that is released in one quarter and
// re-charged in the next is a different animal from one that was simply spent.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsProvision
{
   provisionId: String[1];
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   provisionType: String[1];
   openingBalance: Float[1];
   chargeAmount: Float[0..1];
   utilisedAmount: Float[0..1];
   releasedAmount: Float[0..1];
   closingBalance: Float[1];
   expectedSettlementDate: StrictDate[0..1];
   isDiscounted: Boolean[0..1];
   lineId: String[0..1];

   line: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[0..1];

   // Opening + charge - utilised - released. Should equal `closingBalance`.
   rollForward() { (($this.openingBalance + $this.chargeAmount->orElse(0.0)) - $this.utilisedAmount->orElse(0.0)) - $this.releasedAmount->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   rollForwardCheck() { $this.closingBalance - ((($this.openingBalance + $this.chargeAmount->orElse(0.0)) - $this.utilisedAmount->orElse(0.0)) - $this.releasedAmount->orElse(0.0)) } : Float[1];
   netCharge() { $this.chargeAmount->orElse(0.0) - $this.releasedAmount->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   utilisationPct() { ($this.utilisedAmount->orElse(0.0) * 100.0) / $this.openingBalance } : Float[1];
   isReleasing() { $this.releasedAmount->orElse(0.0) > $this.chargeAmount->orElse(0.0) } : Boolean[1];
}

// FOR: the expected-credit-loss allowance, split by IFRS 9 stage. Stage 1 is twelve-month
// ECL, stages 2 and 3 are lifetime, and the migration between them is what makes a loan book
// look fine one quarter and not the next. `postModelAdjustment` is the overlay a credit
// committee applied because the model had not seen the current situation before, and it is
// held separately precisely so it cannot be mistaken for a modelled number.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsEclAllowance
{
   allowanceId: String[1];
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   eclStage: Integer[1];
   portfolioCode: String[1];
   grossExposureAmount: Float[1];
   twelveMonthEcl: Float[0..1];
   lifetimeEcl: Float[0..1];
   allowanceAmount: Float[1];
   modelCode: String[0..1];
   postModelAdjustment: Float[0..1];
   netExposureId: String[0..1];

   bankingAssets: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBankingBookAsset[*];
   // exposure-agg's net exposure for the same obligor, after collateral. An allowance that
   // ignores the collateral and a net exposure that counts it are two legitimate numbers,
   // and having both on one navigation is the reason for the dependency.
   netExposure: exposure_agg::ExaNetExposure[0..1];

   coverageRatio() { ($this.allowanceAmount * 100.0) / $this.grossExposureAmount } : Float[1];
   modelledAmount() { $this.allowanceAmount - $this.postModelAdjustment->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   overlayPct() { ($this.postModelAdjustment->orElse(0.0) * 100.0) / $this.allowanceAmount } : Float[1];
   isLifetime() { $this.eclStage >= 2 } : Boolean[1];
   isCreditImpaired() { $this.eclStage == 3 } : Boolean[1];
   // What migrating a loan from stage 1 to stage 2 costs, in money: the twelve-month number
   // is replaced by the lifetime one and the difference is charged on the day it moves.
   stageMigrationCost() { $this.lifetimeEcl->orElse(0.0) - $this.twelveMonthEcl->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
}

// ------------------------------------------------------- the equity that balances it

// FOR: the taxonomy of equity. Share capital, share premium, retained earnings, OCI
// reserves, AT1. `isDistributable` and `capitalTier` are the two questions asked of every
// component and they have different answers: a reserve can be regulatory capital and still
// not be payable as a dividend.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsEquityComponent
{
   componentCode: String[1];
   componentName: String[1];
   componentType: String[1];
   capitalTier: String[0..1];
   isDistributable: Boolean[0..1];
   isRecyclable: Boolean[0..1];
   presentationOrder: Integer[0..1];

   balances: firm_balance_sheet::FbsEquityBalance[*];
   ociReserves: firm_balance_sheet::FbsOciReserve[*];

   isCommonEquity() { $this.capitalTier == 'CET1' } : Boolean[1];
   isPayable() { $this.isDistributable->orElse(false) } : Boolean[1];
}

// FOR: one equity component's balance on one statement, with its movement. Split between
// the parent and the minority because a consolidated balance sheet includes subsidiaries the
// group does not wholly own, and the residual belongs to two sets of shareholders.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsEquityBalance
{
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   componentCode: String[1];
   reportingCurrency: String[1];
   openingBalance: Float[1];
   movementAmount: Float[0..1];
   closingBalance: Float[1];
   attributableToParent: Float[0..1];
   nonControllingInterest: Float[0..1];
   lineId: String[0..1];

   statement: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBalanceSheet[0..1];
   component: firm_balance_sheet::FbsEquityComponent[0..1];
   line: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[0..1];

   // Opening + movement should equal closing.
   movementCheck() { $this.closingBalance - ($this.openingBalance + $this.movementAmount->orElse(0.0)) } : Float[1];
   ownershipSplitCheck() { $this.closingBalance - ($this.attributableToParent->orElse($this.closingBalance) + $this.nonControllingInterest->orElse(0.0)) } : Float[1];
   minorityPct() { ($this.nonControllingInterest->orElse(0.0) * 100.0) / $this.closingBalance } : Float[1];
   movementPct() { ($this.movementAmount->orElse(0.0) * 100.0) / $this.openingBalance } : Float[1];
}

// FOR: the reserve where FVOCI movements go to wait. It is the direct consequence of the
// measurement basis: a bond held to collect AND sell moves in value, the move is real, and
// it lands here instead of in profit. `recycledToPl` is what left this reserve when the bond
// was finally sold -- for a debt instrument. For an equity instrument it is permanently zero
// and `isRecyclable` says so, which is the whole of the FVOCI election in two columns.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsOciReserve
{
   reserveId: String[1];
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   reserveType: String[1];
   basisCode: String[0..1];
   grossReserve: Float[1];
   deferredTax: Float[0..1];
   netReserve: Float[1];
   recycledToPl: Float[0..1];
   isRecyclable: Boolean[0..1];
   componentCode: String[0..1];

   basis: firm_balance_sheet::FbsMeasurementBasis[0..1];
   component: firm_balance_sheet::FbsEquityComponent[0..1];

   taxCheck() { $this.netReserve - ($this.grossReserve - $this.deferredTax->orElse(0.0)) } : Float[1];
   effectiveTaxPct() { ($this.deferredTax->orElse(0.0) * 100.0) / $this.grossReserve } : Float[1];
   isLoss() { $this.netReserve < 0.0 } : Boolean[1];
   isTrapped() { $this.isRecyclable->orElse(true) == false } : Boolean[1];
}

// FOR: the one line of equity the income statement writes into. Opening plus the profit for
// the period less dividends declared plus everything else equals closing, and
// `pnlRunTotal.totalPnl()` is where the middle term is supposed to have come from. Where the
// two disagree, either the P&L was restated or the equity was, and the disagreement is more
// informative than either number alone.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsRetainedEarnings
{
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   reportingCurrency: String[1];
   openingRetained: Float[1];
   profitForPeriod: Float[1];
   dividendsDeclared: Float[0..1];
   otherMovements: Float[0..1];
   closingRetained: Float[1];
   pnlAttributionId: String[0..1];
   isVerified: Boolean[0..1];

   statement: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBalanceSheet[0..1];
   // The firm's whole day of P&L, as one row, from pnl-attribution's `~groupBy` view.
   pnlRunTotal: pnl_attribution::PnlRunTotal[0..1];

   rollForward() { (($this.openingRetained + $this.profitForPeriod) - $this.dividendsDeclared->orElse(0.0)) + $this.otherMovements->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   rollForwardCheck() { $this.closingRetained - ((($this.openingRetained + $this.profitForPeriod) - $this.dividendsDeclared->orElse(0.0)) + $this.otherMovements->orElse(0.0)) } : Float[1];
   payoutRatio() { ($this.dividendsDeclared->orElse(0.0) * 100.0) / $this.profitForPeriod } : Float[1];
   isLossMaking() { $this.profitForPeriod < 0.0 } : Boolean[1];
   growthPct() { (($this.closingRetained - $this.openingRetained) * 100.0) / $this.openingRetained } : Float[1];
}

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- control

// FOR: a manual journal against a line. Every balance sheet has some, and what the class is
// FOR is making them visible: who raised it, who approved it, and whether it has been
// reversed. A live adjustment with no approver is the row an auditor is looking for.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsAccountingAdjustment
{
   adjustmentId: String[1];
   lineId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   adjustmentType: String[1];
   adjustmentAmount: Float[1];
   reason: String[0..1];
   raisedBy: String[0..1];
   raisedOn: StrictDate[0..1];
   approvedBy: String[0..1];
   approvedOn: StrictDate[0..1];
   reversedOn: StrictDate[0..1];

   line: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[0..1];

   isApproved() { $this.approvedOn->isNotEmpty() } : Boolean[1];
   isLive() { $this.reversedOn->isEmpty() } : Boolean[1];
   isUnapprovedAndLive() { $this.approvedOn->isEmpty() && $this.reversedOn->isEmpty() } : Boolean[1];
   absoluteAmount() { $this.adjustmentAmount->abs() } : Float[1];
}

// FOR: a stated equality that did not hold. Assets against liabilities-plus-equity is the
// obvious one; the class is generic (`checkType`, `leftAmount`, `rightAmount`) because the
// same shape catches gross derivatives against netted derivatives, HQLA against the LCR
// numerator, and retained earnings against the P&L run, and a reader wants all of them in
// one place rather than four differently-named tables.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsBalanceCheck
{
   checkId: String[1];
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   reportingCurrency: String[1];
   checkType: String[1];
   leftAmount: Float[1];
   rightAmount: Float[1];
   differenceAmount: Float[0..1];
   toleranceAmount: Float[0..1];
   severity: String[0..1];
   detectedAt: DateTime[0..1];
   resolvedOn: StrictDate[0..1];
   owner: String[0..1];

   statement: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBalanceSheet[0..1];

   computedDifference() { $this.leftAmount - $this.rightAmount } : Float[1];
   // Stated difference against recomputed. Two ways to be wrong, and they disagree.
   differenceCheck() { $this.differenceAmount->orElse($this.leftAmount - $this.rightAmount) - ($this.leftAmount - $this.rightAmount) } : Float[1];
   breachRatio() { ($this.leftAmount - $this.rightAmount)->abs() / $this.toleranceAmount->orElse(1.0) } : Float[1];
   isWithinTolerance() { ($this.leftAmount - $this.rightAmount)->abs() <= $this.toleranceAmount->orElse(0.0) } : Boolean[1];
   isOpen() { $this.resolvedOn->isEmpty() } : Boolean[1];
   isBlocking() { $this.severity == 'BLOCKING' && $this.resolvedOn->isEmpty() } : Boolean[1];
}

// FOR: one role's acceptance of a statement. An unattested balance sheet is unread rather
// than wrong; `withdrawnOn` exists because an attestation can be taken back, and a statement
// whose only attestation has been withdrawn is in a worse state than one that never had one.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsAttestation
{
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   roleCode: String[1];
   attestedBy: String[0..1];
   attestedAt: DateTime[0..1];
   attestationStatus: String[1];
   commentary: String[0..1];
   withdrawnOn: StrictDate[0..1];

   statement: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBalanceSheet[0..1];

   isCurrent() { $this.withdrawnOn->isEmpty() } : Boolean[1];
   isAccepted() { $this.attestationStatus == 'ACCEPTED' && $this.withdrawnOn->isEmpty() } : Boolean[1];
}

// ============================================================================================
// THE AGGREGATION SHAPE -- four classes rooted at `~groupBy` VIEWS, not tables
// ============================================================================================
// Each of the four is one row per group over `fbs.FBS_LINE_ITEM`, at four different widths.
// Their primary key IS the grouping, so navigating into one crosses into a GROUP BY and never
// into another line. A group with no lines FORMS NO GROUP and is absent rather than zero: a
// category with nothing in it on a date does not appear, and a downstream report that must
// print every category on every day drives from `FbsCategory` and outer-joins.
//
// Every sum is `Float[0..1]`, because a sum over a nullable column is nullable, so every
// derived property below `->orElse(0.0)` before it does arithmetic. `count()` is Integer.

// FOR: the statement as it is actually printed -- one row per category per statement, which
// is the line a reader sees. Grouped from the line table, so it can never disagree with it.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsCategoryTotal
{
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   reportingCurrency: String[1];
   categoryCode: String[1];
   lineCount: Integer[1];
   totalCarrying: Float[0..1];
   totalGross: Float[0..1];
   totalImpairment: Float[0..1];
   totalPriorCarrying: Float[0..1];
   largestLine: Float[0..1];
   smallestLine: Float[0..1];

   statement: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBalanceSheet[0..1];
   category: firm_balance_sheet::FbsCategory[0..1];
   lines: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[*];

   movement() { $this.totalCarrying->orElse(0.0) - $this.totalPriorCarrying->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   movementPct() { (($this.totalCarrying->orElse(0.0) - $this.totalPriorCarrying->orElse(0.0)) * 100.0) / $this.totalPriorCarrying->orElse(1.0) } : Float[1];
   averageLine() { $this.totalCarrying->orElse(0.0) / $this.lineCount->toFloat() } : Float[1];
   coverageRatio() { $this.totalImpairment->orElse(0.0) / $this.totalGross->orElse(1.0) } : Float[1];
   // A total of zero built from two enormous opposite numbers is not a total of zero in any
   // sense a reader cares about, which is what max and min are here for.
   spread() { $this.largestLine->orElse(0.0) - $this.smallestLine->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   concentrationPct() { ($this.largestLine->orElse(0.0) * 100.0) / $this.totalCarrying->orElse(1.0) } : Float[1];
}

// FOR: the measurement-basis disclosure -- how much of each side of the sheet is at
// amortised cost, at FVOCI and at FVTPL. Grouped by basis AND side because "how much is fair
// valued" is a different question for assets and for liabilities and the netted answer is
// meaningless.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsBasisTotal
{
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   reportingCurrency: String[1];
   basisCode: String[1];
   side: String[1];
   lineCount: Integer[1];
   totalCarrying: Float[0..1];
   totalGross: Float[0..1];
   totalImpairment: Float[0..1];
   largestLine: Float[0..1];

   basis: firm_balance_sheet::FbsMeasurementBasis[0..1];
   lines: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[*];

   averageLine() { $this.totalCarrying->orElse(0.0) / $this.lineCount->toFloat() } : Float[1];
   netOfImpairment() { $this.totalGross->orElse(0.0) - $this.totalImpairment->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   isFairValueBasis() { $this.basisCode == 'FVTPL' || $this.basisCode == 'FVOCI' } : Boolean[1];
   concentrationPct() { ($this.largestLine->orElse(0.0) * 100.0) / $this.totalCarrying->orElse(1.0) } : Float[1];
}

// FOR: the book boundary in money -- trading book against banking book, per side. This is the
// row a regulator reads first, because a position that migrated across the boundary changed
// its capital treatment without changing anything about itself.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsBookTotal
{
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   bookCode: String[1];
   side: String[1];
   lineCount: Integer[1];
   totalCarrying: Float[0..1];
   totalPriorCarrying: Float[0..1];
   largestLine: Float[0..1];

   book: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBookClassification[0..1];
   lines: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[*];

   movement() { $this.totalCarrying->orElse(0.0) - $this.totalPriorCarrying->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   averageLine() { $this.totalCarrying->orElse(0.0) / $this.lineCount->toFloat() } : Float[1];
   isTradingBook() { $this.bookCode == 'TRADING' } : Boolean[1];
   dayMovePct() { (($this.totalCarrying->orElse(0.0) - $this.totalPriorCarrying->orElse(0.0)) * 100.0) / $this.totalPriorCarrying->orElse(1.0) } : Float[1];
}

// FOR: the balance check itself, computed rather than stated. Three rows per statement --
// ASSET, LIABILITY, EQUITY -- grouped straight from the line table, so the sum of the last
// two against the first is the identity with nothing in between it and the data.
// `FbsBalanceSheet.totalAssets` is what was published; this is what the lines say.
Class firm_balance_sheet::FbsSideTotal
{
   institutionId: String[1];
   asOfDate: StrictDate[1];
   reportingCurrency: String[1];
   side: String[1];
   lineCount: Integer[1];
   totalCarrying: Float[0..1];
   totalGross: Float[0..1];
   totalImpairment: Float[0..1];
   totalPriorCarrying: Float[0..1];

   statement: firm_balance_sheet::FbsBalanceSheet[0..1];
   lines: firm_balance_sheet::FbsLineItem[*];

   movement() { $this.totalCarrying->orElse(0.0) - $this.totalPriorCarrying->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   averageLine() { $this.totalCarrying->orElse(0.0) / $this.lineCount->toFloat() } : Float[1];
   netOfImpairment() { $this.totalGross->orElse(0.0) - $this.totalImpairment->orElse(0.0) } : Float[1];
   isAssetSide() { $this.side == 'ASSET' } : Boolean[1];
}
